From 5034a995e8fe41cb33f0920cbc73c73c4e625c2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:14:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] SEQ MIDI OUT: mutes and solo as CC 103; a silent track
 sends no note-on

A track is silent as its sound is: its MUTE (P_MUTE), or GLO's SOLO held
on another track (perf_solo, as ui_layer.c glo_sounding; not while
perf_kill turns the layer's effects off). A silent track sends no
note-on; its note-offs and its step CC 102 go on. Turning silent with
notes held: CC 123 on its channel first.

CC 103 on the track's channel (T1..T6 CHANNEL) says it: 127 silent,
0 sounding. Sent when it changes (compared every audio block with what
was sent last, so every source counts: keys, solo, launches, loads, a
channel change), for all six right after Start, on every bar while
playing (16 1/16 steps, either clock), when SEQ MIDI OUT turns ON and
when USB comes up. Nothing while SEQ MIDI OUT is OFF.

tests/seqmidi_test.c: cases 1-8 of docs/FIRMWARE-MUTE.md (mute while a
note sounds, sounding again, Start, the bars, OFF, T2 on channel 10,
solo, a muted track's step CC).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01257TywRk7Y9DD2HfKqtetj
